<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Support – <%= botName %></title>
    <meta name="description" content="Get help with <%= botName %>: verification, moderation appeals, staff applications, data requests and bug reports.">
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg: #0e0f13;
            --panel: #16181f;
            --panel-border: #262a35;
            --accent: #5865F2;
            --accent-hover: #7983f5;
            --text: #e7e9ee;
            --text-dim: #9aa0ac;
        }
        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        body {
            margin: 0;
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            font: 16px/1.7 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        }
        .wrap { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 20px 80px; }
        .topnav { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 28px; }
        .topnav a {
            color: var(--text-dim);
            text-decoration: none;
            font-size: 14px;
            padding: 6px 14px;
            border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
            border-radius: 999px;
        }
        .topnav a:hover { color: var(--text); border-color: var(--accent); }
        .topnav a.active { color: #fff; background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
        h1 { font-size: 34px; margin: 0 0 6px; letter-spacing: -0.5px; }
        .lead { color: var(--text-dim); margin: 0 0 28px; }
        h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 38px 0 14px; }
        p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
        a { color: var(--accent-hover); }
        strong { color: #fff; }
        .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }
        .card {
            background: var(--panel);
            border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 20px 22px;
        }
        .card h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 17px; }
        .card p { margin: 0 0 10px; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; }
        .card p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
        .btn {
            display: inline-block;
            background: var(--accent);
            color: #fff;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: 600;
            font-size: 14px;
            padding: 8px 16px;
            border-radius: 8px;
        }
        .btn:hover { background: var(--accent-hover); }
        details {
            background: var(--panel);
            border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
            border-radius: 12px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            padding: 0 22px;
        }
        summary {
            cursor: pointer;
            font-weight: 600;
            padding: 15px 0;
            list-style: none;
            color: #fff;
        }
        summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
        summary::before { content: '+'; display: inline-block; width: 22px; color: var(--accent-hover); font-weight: 700; }
        details[open] summary::before { content: '–'; }
        details .answer { padding: 0 0 16px 22px; color: var(--text); }
        details .answer ul, details .answer ol { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 22px; }
        details .answer li { margin: 4px 0; }
        .note {
            border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
            background: var(--panel);
            border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
            padding: 14px 20px;
            margin-top: 28px;
            font-size: 15px;
            color: var(--text-dim);
        }
        footer { margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--panel-border); color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 14px; }
        @media (max-width: 600px) { h1 { font-size: 28px; } }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
    <nav class="topnav">
        <a class="active" href="/support">Support</a>
        <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
    </nav>

    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="lead">Need help with <%= botName %>? Here’s how to reach us and answers to the most common questions.</p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
            <h3>Discord server</h3>
            <p>The fastest way to get help. Ask in the server and a staff member will pick it up.</p>
            <% if (supportUrl) { %>
            <p><a class="btn" href="<%= supportUrl %>" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Join the server</a></p>
            <% } %>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
            <h3>Message the bot</h3>
            <p>Send <%= botName %> a direct message. It’s relayed privately to staff, who reply to you in your DMs. Keep your DMs open so you can get the reply.</p>
        </div>
        <% if (contactEmail) { %>
        <div class="card">
            <h3>Email</h3>
            <p>For anything you’d rather not post in the server, such as privacy or data requests.</p>
            <p><a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a></p>
        </div>
        <% } %>
    </div>

    <h2>Common questions</h2>

    <details>
        <summary>I can’t verify</summary>
        <div class="answer">
            <ol>
                <li>Make sure you’ve joined the server first.</li>
                <li>Open the <a href="/verify">verification page</a> and sign in with Discord.</li>
                <li>Complete the CAPTCHA and tick the rules agreement, then submit.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>If the CAPTCHA doesn’t show up, a privacy extension, ad blocker or VPN may be blocking it. Try turning it off for this page or using another browser. Still stuck? Contact staff with a short description of what you see.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>I was warned, muted, kicked or banned and think it’s a mistake</summary>
        <div class="answer">
            <p>
                Tell us what happened by DMing the bot or asking in the server (if you’re banned, DM the bot or
                email us). Include your Discord username and what you think went wrong. Staff will review it.
                Automatic flags and actions can be wrong, and they’re not a final judgment about you. See the
                <a href="/terms#moderation">Terms</a> for how moderation works.
            </p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>A command isn’t working or the bot is offline</summary>
        <div class="answer">
            <ul>
                <li>Use <strong>/help</strong> to see what’s available, and check you have permission for the command you’re trying.</li>
                <li>Wait a moment and try again. Discord can lag, and the bot restarts after updates.</li>
                <li>If the bot is down or the website says it’s in maintenance, that’s usually temporary. If it lasts, let staff know.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>How do confessions work?</summary>
        <div class="answer">
            <p>
                Confessions are posted publicly without your name, but they are not anonymous to staff, who can see
                the author so abuse can be handled. If you see a confession that breaks the rules, report it to staff.
                More in the <a href="/terms#confessions">Terms</a> and the <a href="/privacy#collect">Privacy Policy</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>Staff applications</summary>
        <div class="answer">
            <p>
                You can apply for <a href="/mod-apps/apply">moderator</a> or
                <a href="/apply-co-owner">co-owner</a> when applications are open. The owners review
                them, and not every application gets a position. If you’ve been waiting a while or
                something looks broken, ask in the server.
            </p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>I want to see, correct or delete my data</summary>
        <div class="answer">
            <p>
                Contact us using the options above and say what you need. We may ask you to confirm you control the
                Discord account first. Leaving the server doesn’t delete your data automatically, so you do need to
                ask. Some records, such as moderation history, may be kept for safety reasons. Details are in the
                <a href="/privacy#rights">Privacy Policy</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details>
        <summary>I found a bug or have a suggestion</summary>
        <div class="answer">
            <p>
                Tell staff in the server. The most useful reports say what you did, what you expected, what happened
                instead, and roughly when. If it’s a security problem, please DM the bot or email us instead of
                posting it publicly.
            </p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <div class="note">
        If someone is in danger or a message involves a serious threat, report it to Discord as well:
        <a href="https://discord.com/safety" rel="noopener" target="_blank">discord.com/safety</a>.
        Staff here can’t act on things that happen outside the server.
    </div>

    <footer>
        <a href="/support">Support</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
        <br>
        <%= botName %> is an independent community project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Discord Inc.
    </footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
